in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance
in @mirror
in @mirror/bench

# @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance — the OPERATIONAL
# HALF of the second ouroboros bite. The auto-fracture that emits a
# re-bench morphism when cold compile time regresses past tolerance.
#
# Tick 43 / second ouroboros bite (operational half). Sibling to
# @epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance (declarative
# half; landed in the same tick).
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; fourth instance, operational half) ===
#
# Per the established property+fracture bilateral discipline:
# - Declarative half: the predicate (@epistemologic/property/<name>)
# - Operational half: the fracture body via splinter(ast)
#                     (@kintsugi/fracture/<name>)
#
# When the property's verdict fails on an opacity (a crate at the
# current substrate-pull tick where cold compile regressed against
# baseline), this fracture body emits a morphism whose splinter(ast)
# names a re-bench action.
#
# === The re-bench discipline ===
#
# Per Taut's analysis: yesterday's 38-min hang would have been caught
# at the pre-push gate if cold_compile baseline crystal had existed.
# This fracture body composes that future-state:
#
#   When property fails (current cold_compile > baseline × (1 + tol)):
#     emit morphism { content: splinter(ast) { ... } } that:
#       - clears the substrate's incremental compile cache for `crate`
#       - re-runs cold_compile against `crate` with measured runtime
#       - records new bench_crystal at @mirror/bench altitude
#       - if new runtime still > baseline × (1 + tol):
#           refuse push (substrate-pull-correct hold)
#         else:
#           the new crystal becomes the chain's next predecessor
#
# === Composes with @mirror/bench ===
#
# The emitted morphism IS a re-bench operation. Bench records the
# re-run; the predecessor-chain grows; @loop.bind cascades the pact-
# verification at the next iteration.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   pre-push gate              Git hooks with cargo audit + cargo
#                              test; this fracture body lifts the
#                              gate to substrate-decl altitude.
#   regression-bench bisect    git bisect over perf crystals; the
#                              predecessor-OID chain at @mirror/bench
#                              enables substrate-altitude bisection.
#   property-based shrinking   QuickCheck-style shrinking;
#                              substrate's re-bench IS shrinking at
#                              perf altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_
#               tolerance.mirror (the DECLARATIVE HALF this fracture
#               body composes); shards/mirror/bench.mirror (the bench
#               substrate-decl this fracture body's morphism feeds).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       this fracture body is the operational half of
#                       the second ouroboros bite),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53 pattern; this is the operational half of
#                       the fourth instance),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                       (the substrate's quote primitive; this body
#                       discharges via splinter(ast) declaratively,
#                       no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-loop-as-monad]] (#88; the re-
#                       bench IS one @loop iteration at the perf
#                       altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity, morphism,
#                       bench_crystal are typed carriers).
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror
#                  (the declarative half),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (the bench substrate-decl whose
#                  regress_check feeds back to the chain walk),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (SIBLING THIRD INSTANCE of the bilateral pattern;
#                  this shard is the FOURTH),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                  driver; active_pass reads this fracture body when
#                  composing the per-pulse candidate morphism_set),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; opacity,
#                  location, transparency, verdict, splinter(ast)).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror`
# declares `@kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/programming/bencher-criterion-2014
source @arxiv/programming/claessen-hughes-2000

glass @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance {
  focus cold_compile_within_tolerance
  project cold_compile_within_tolerance
  split cold_compile_within_tolerance
  shift cold_compile_within_tolerance
  settle cold_compile_within_tolerance
}

# === resolve_cold_compile_regression action (fracture body) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Reads an opacity (one element of
# `cold_compile_within_tolerance(c, baseline, current, tol)
# .failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map); emits a candidate morphism
# the kintsugi loop proposes through query_phi.
#
# The morphism's content field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at @meta/ast altitude: the re-bench action on the offending crate.
# Per [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]: splinter(ast)
# IS the substrate's quote primitive; the re-bench rides the same
# carrier as every other AST rewrite.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE via splinter(ast). No Rust
# manipulation; the substrate's compiler verifies the construction is
# deterministic and well-typed.
resolve_cold_compile_regression(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance
out resolve_cold_compile_regression
